notices included in a selected runtime asset.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AppImage type2 runtime (Linux AppImage packages)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Linux AppImage packages embed a source-built AppImage type2 runtime instead of
the upstream release download.

Upstream: https://github.com/AppImage/type2-runtime
Commit:   fedfad51acc2860b2916a1eef32ba4a500ff31ef
License:  MIT; the unchanged upstream license text is in
          scripts/appimage-runtime/LICENSE.type2-runtime

AioLM applies two patches, distributed under the same MIT license, from
scripts/appimage-runtime/patches/:

- 0001-rm_recursive-pass-positive-nftw-fd_limit.patch
- 0002-extract-and-run-use-a-per-instance-directory.patch

The pinned inputs and expected runtime digest are recorded in
scripts/appimage-runtime/pins.conf. The runtime is built in an Alpine Linux
3.21.0 minirootfs using upstream's build scripts; the exact Alpine package set
is recorded in scripts/appimage-runtime/apk.lock.

As in upstream's release, the runtime statically links the following
components, each distributed under its own license:

- libfuse 3.15.0 (LGPL-2.1)
- squashfuse 0.5.2 (BSD-2-Clause)
- zstd 1.5.6 (BSD-3-Clause or GPL-2.0)
- zlib 1.3.2 (Zlib)
- mimalloc 2.1.7 (MIT)
- musl 1.2.5 (MIT)

Their exact sources are the pinned upstream tarballs fetched by upstream's
install-dependencies.sh at the commit above and the Alpine packages listed in
scripts/appimage-runtime/apk.lock.
